      "extract": "There are two different $q$-analogue of the Airy function. One is called the Ramanujan function which appears in [@Ramanujan]. Ismail [@Is] pointed out that the Ramanujan function can be considered as a $q$-analogue of the Airy function. The other one is called the $q$-Airy function which is obtained by K. Kajiwara, T. Masuda, M. Noumi, Y. Ohta and Y. Yamada [@KMNOY]. In this section, we see the properties of these",
